<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica provisional financing figures for March 97.</title>
<headline>SAfrica provisional financing figures for March 97.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financing of 2,466.2 million rand was obtained in government bonds while net short-term loans decreased by 470.4 million rand during March this year, the South African Finance Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>This brought the total financing for that month to 2,341.1, the department said in a statement.</p>
<p>			     March 1997		 April 1996 -</p>
<p>							    March 1997</p>
<p>			     (R'million)</p>
<p>Government bonds and</p>
<p>    debentures	   2,466.2		    36,309.5</p>
<p>Short-term (net)</p>
<p>    Bridging bonds	   0.0		    -3,616.5</p>
<p>    Tender Bills	     0.0		     3,600.0</p>
<p>Corporation for</p>
<p>     Public Deposits    -470.4		     1,966.8</p>
<p>Foreign loans		  0.0		     2,831.0</p>
<p>			    --------		    --------</p>
<p>    Total financing    2,341.1		    43,038.6</p>
<p>Government bonds and debentures to the amount of 16,648 million rand and foreign loans to the amount of 1,899 million rand were redeemed during April 1996 to March 1997, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
